# data/ is ~1.5 GB. The source docking files are 695 MB each and the frozen CV splits
# are 112 MB, so nothing under data/ is tracked by default -- see CLAUDE.md, which flags
# deciding .gitignore vs git-LFS as a prerequisite to committing anything here.
#
# The exception is data/reference/: a few hundred KB of frozen MiniMol embeddings that
# src/verify_trunk.py checks the trainable trunk against. That fixture is only useful if
# it travels with the code, so it is un-ignored below.
data/*
!data/reference/
!data/*.meta.json

# TRACKED from 2026-08-25, reversing the exclusion that used to sit here. The reason it was
# excluded -- "regenerable in ~2.5 min from src/split.py" -- turned out not to hold: rdkit
# shifts Morgan fingerprint details between releases, so regenerating on another machine
# produces a DIFFERENT partition and a different split_sha256, which makes every number
# incomparable. They therefore have to be copied rather than rebuilt, and once that is true
# they may as well travel with the code.
#
# The repo now runs on TamIA as well as rabelais, and moving 141 MB by scp on every clone was
# both error-prone and the slowest part of setting the cluster up. 141 MB is permanent history
# growth; it is accepted deliberately. The largest single file, fingerprints.npy at 81 MB, is
# under GitHub's 100 MB hard limit -- keep it that way.
!data/ampc_subset_331k.csv
!data/splits/

# NOT tracked, and should not be: 4.5 GB, and genuinely regenerable in ~3.5 min from
# src/featurize.py, which depends only on the CSV above rather than on an rdkit version.
data/features/

# Recreated by `uv sync` from the tracked pyproject.toml + uv.lock. ~5 GB with the CUDA
# wheels, and it is platform-specific -- it must never travel to another cluster.
.venv/

# The minimol 1.3.4 wheel is 19 MB because it carries the pretrained weights. Kept as a
# hedge against PyPI, but too big to track -- see NOTES on rebuilding it.
vendor/

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Training run artifacts: a 34 MB checkpoint plus predictions per run, and the 5x2 grid
# makes 10 of them. meta.json records everything needed to reproduce a run, so the
# artifacts themselves are regenerable.
outputs/

# wandb and SLURM leave these behind; logs live in /home/ethan2/logs/ by convention.
wandb/
*.out
*.err
